// @run
// @log 9
// CLOSED (#1803) — this was `xfail-false-reject-call-result-union-arg.vl`, and the prefix is
// dropped per this directory's README ("when it closes, drop the prefix and flip the file to
// @run + @log"). A declared struct produced by a CALL, passed into an INLINE union parameter.
// Sound program, refused with `emitProgram: ref valtype with no interned shape`.
//
// WHAT IT WAS, in the terms the old header had already narrowed it to. Its layers 1-3 were
// right: the struct table is EMPTY because `collectS` skips a `TypeDecl` the emitter's
// `uVariants` claims, and the kind fell through to `"struct"` because `retVariantFlag` reads
// the CHECKER's `cVariantMemberTyIxs` — which "does not cover this shape". What no attempt
// tried was FILLING that registry: `collectU` feeds `uVariants` from BOTH union spellings
// while pass 0b's `UnionDecl` arm fed `cVariantMemberTyIxs` from one, so the inline spelling
// left the two halves of the compiler disagreeing about the same fact.
// `annRegisterVariantMembers` (typecheck) registers a DECLARED struct member of an inline
// union annotation exactly as the declaration route does, and everything downstream — the rep
// tree's `rtOfObj` discriminator, `nodeTyIsVariant`, `nodeTyIsStruct` — moves together.
//
// THAT IS WHY THE OLD B184 DEAD END FAILED and this does not. Flipping only the KIND made 7 of
// 10 repros compile into INVALID MODULES: "the signature now says variant while the body still
// BUILDS the plain struct". Registering the member moves the producer too, so the value IS the
// variant — the header's own condition for a real fix ("either the arm gets a struct row, or
// the producer builds the variant").
//
// The B185 conflict it feared does not arise either: `types/variant-as-value.vl` pins a
// concrete variant riding `(ref $uVarHeap[vi])` directly, which is exactly what this program
// now does. No struct row is minted for `A` anywhere.
//
// The BINDING twin (`call-result-union-binding.vl`) closed later, on the SAME registry: its
// union's two arms are SAME-SHAPE, so the annotation route deduped them to one member and
// returned before ever reaching `annRegisterVariantMembers`. Registering the dropped pair at
// the dedup itself is the whole of that fix — see that file.
type A = { tag: i32, v: i32 }
function f(x: A | i32) {
  if x is A { return x.v }
  0
}
function mkA(): A { return { tag: 1, v: 9 } }
print(f(mkA()))
